.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a substring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function reads the file stream
.I fp
line by line, searching for lines containing
.I search_str.
Matching lines are copied into a dynamically-allocated array of strings,
whose address is stored in
.I *matches.
The caller is responsible for freeing each matched string and the array
itself.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
